---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { project, formatDate } from '../lib/content';
---

<Base
  title="About the community project"
  description="Meet Better Pasay’s community maintainer, learn our information standards, and find out how to contribute sources or report corrections."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="About Better Pasay"
    title="A city guide. A shared effort."
    description="Public information should be easier to find, understand and verify. Better Pasay brings our city, its services, and its public records a little closer to everyone."
  />
  <div class="container about-layout">
    <div class="about-content">
      <section>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why we’re here</p>
        <h2>
          Less searching.
          <br />
          More understanding.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Better Pasay brings service links and public records into one
          resident-friendly guide. We write short community summaries and send
          you to the original source for the details.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is an independent, community-led project for Pasay City, Metro
          Manila. It is not an official government website. We do not process
          applications, collect fees or speak for the city government.
        </p>
        <p>
          The project is registered in the{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/jmacj/better-lgu-directory">
            Better LGU Directory
          </a>{' '}
          through{' '}
          <a href="https://github.com/jmacj/better-lgu-directory/pull/319">
            PR #319
          </a>
          . Directory registration does not imply government endorsement or
          formal affiliation with BetterGov.ph.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="standards">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our information standards</p>
        <h2>Useful information earns trust.</h2>
        <ol class="standards-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Start at the source.</strong>
            <p>
              Use public government pages and documents. For a separate domain,
              trace its link from an official city page.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Show what was checked, and when.</strong>
            <p>
              Each entry has a source and a verification date. A document’s
              edition or reporting period is kept separate from its publication
              date.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Be clear about the gaps.</strong>
            <p>
              We label limited reviews and omit unverified requirements, fees,
              contacts and statistics. A checked source may still change or
              contain errors.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Keep corrections open.</strong>
            <p>
              Anyone can suggest a correction with a supporting source. Changes
              are reviewed through the public repository.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </section>
      <section id="contribute">
        <p class="eyebrow">Make the guide better</p>
        <h2>You don’t have to write code.</h2>
        <p>
          Help check a source, improve a Filipino search term, test on your
          phone, or explain where a page is confusing.
        </p>
        <div class="contribution-steps">
          <div>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Find something to improve</h3>
            <p>Note the page or service and what is missing or incorrect.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Bring a public source</h3>
            <p>
              Include the original URL and the date you checked it. Explain the
              proposed correction.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Open an issue or pull request</h3>
            <p>
              Use GitHub to share your suggestion with the community maintainer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="notice">
          <strong>Keep reports public and safe to share.</strong> Do not include
          IDs, medical records, private phone numbers, application documents or
          other personal information in GitHub issues.
        </p>
        <div class="inline-actions">
          <a
            class="button"
            href={`${project.issues}/new?template=content-correction.yml`}
          >
            Report a correction <Icon name="external" size={18} />
          </a>
          <a href={`${project.repository}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>
            Read the contribution guide ↗
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="small">
          GitHub requires an account to submit issues or pull requests. For
          government concerns, use the{' '}
          <a href="https://pasay.gov.ph/contact-us/">
            city’s official contact page
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="credits">
        <p class="eyebrow">Sources & image credits</p>
        <h2>Public knowledge. Proper credit.</h2>
        <p>
          Service summaries link to Pasay City Government’s original guides and
          the 2026 Citizen’s Charter. City and barangay pages identify their
          official sources, census years, and review dates. Explore{' '}
          <a href="/documents/">the document library</a> and{' '}
          <a href="/city/#sources">our city sources</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The homepage photograph of the Mall of Asia complex is by{' '}
          <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Lawrence_ruiz">
            Lawrence Ruiz
          </a>
          , taken 24 May 2016.{' '}
          <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:View_of_Pasay_City_at_SM_Mall_of_Asia.tif">
            Original photograph
          </a>
          ,{' '}
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">
            CC BY-SA 4.0
          </a>
          . Converted to WebP, displayed with a crop and color overlay; the
          photograph retains its original license.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Manila Bay sunset photograph is by Patrick Roque, taken 31
          December 2017 from the Mall of Asia seaside.{' '}
          <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manila_Bay_sunset_-_from_Mall_of_Asia_seaside_(Pasay)(2017-12-31).jpg">
            Original photograph
          </a>
          ,{' '}
          <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/">
            CC BY-SA 4.0
          </a>
          . Resized, converted to WebP, and cropped for display. Photographs are
          historical views, not live imagery.
        </p>
        <p>
          Manrope is locally hosted under the{' '}
          <a href="/fonts/OFL.txt">SIL Open Font License</a>. The design takes
          inspiration from the{' '}
          <a href="https://lgu.bettergov.ph/">Better LGU community</a>; no other
          portal’s code, branding, or locality data has been copied.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <aside class="maintainer-card">
      <span class="maintainer-monogram" aria-hidden="true">
        bp.
      </span>
      <p class="eyebrow">Community maintained</p>
      <h2>@slvdrvncntjvr</h2>
      <p>Project maintainer</p>
      <a href={project.maintainer}>View GitHub profile ↗</a>
      <hr />
      <p>
        <span class="status-dot"></span> <strong>Work in Progress</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        A growing city guide, with sourced services, official documents,
        government information, and all 201 barangays.
      </p>
      <p class="small">
        Initial source review
        <br />
        <time datetime={project.checkedAt}>
          {formatDate(project.checkedAt)}
        </time>
      </p>
      <a href={project.repository}>Explore the source code ↗</a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Base>
